  "prompt": "Is the family home deductible from the gross estate, and up to how much?",
  "runtimeCommit": "d71b913ddf39726234dd02d858fac3e5275e865b",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, the family home is deductible from the gross estate, with a maximum deduction of up to P10,000,000.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nThe deduction of the family home from the gross estate can significantly lower the estate tax liability, making it easier for heirs to manage the estate. This provision is particularly beneficial for families, as it recognizes the importance of the family home in the context of estate planning and tax obligations.",
